            <fieldText>&lt;p style=&quot;color:#c23934;background:#fdf3f2;border-left:4px solid #c23934;padding:10px 12px;border-radius:2px&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This quote could not be accepted. Its status has not been changed.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The most common cause is that the selected BAN is not valid for this quote. A BAN must belong to the same account, DE entity, currency, and invoice frequency as the quote.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;What to do: Click Finish, then click on the Assign BAN button and select another BAN from the list if present, else create a new BAN for this Quote, then try again.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If the BAN looks correct, share the technical details below with your administrator.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;color:#706e6b;background:#f4f6f9;border-left:4px solid #c9ced6;padding:10px 12px;border-radius:2px;font-size:12px&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;{!$Flow.FaultMessage}&lt;/p&gt;</fieldText>
